From: GA36 FW <ga36@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] 0007 ga36 force pll ddr0

Use PLL5 (PLL_DDR0) instead of PLL11 (PLL_DDR1) for DRAM initialization.
The vendor boot0 uses PLL_DDR0. On the specific GA36-MB V1.2 silicon,
PLL11 appears to be unstable or defective, causing a hard fault during
DRAM initialization in the SPL.

---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun8i_a33.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun8i_a33.c
@@ -302,10 +302,10 @@
 			(struct sunxi_mctl_com_reg *)SUNXI_DRAM_COM_BASE;
 
 	clrsetbits_le32(&ccm->dram_pll_cfg, CCM_DRAMPLL_CFG_SRC_MASK,
-			CCM_DRAMPLL_CFG_SRC_PLL11);
+			CCM_DRAMPLL_CFG_SRC_PLL5);
 
-	clock_set_pll11(CONFIG_DRAM_CLK * 1000000 * DRAM_CLK_MUL,
-			DRAM_SIGMA_DELTA_ENABLE);
+	clock_set_pll5(CONFIG_DRAM_CLK * 1000000 * DRAM_CLK_MUL,
+		       DRAM_SIGMA_DELTA_ENABLE);
 
 	clrsetbits_le32(&ccm->dram_clk_cfg, CCM_DRAMCLK_CFG_DIV_MASK,
 			CCM_DRAMCLK_CFG_DIV(DRAM_CLK_DIV) |
